{"resource":{"id":"go-interview-questions","title":"Go \u2014 Interview Questions","category":"Programming","difficulty":"Intermediate","readingTime":"26 min","pages":54,"lastUpdated":"February 2026","tags":["Programming","Go","Concurrency"],"heroImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1461749280684-dccba630e2f6?w=1800&q=80","heroSubtitle":"A 300+ question Go interview handbook \u2014 fundamentals, concurrency, backend design, HR rounds, and real interview scenarios with model answers."},"toc":[{"id":"objectives","label":"Learning Objectives"},{"id":"s1","label":"1. Go Fundamentals"},{"id":"s2","label":"2. Variables & Types"},{"id":"s3","label":"3. Functions"},{"id":"s4","label":"4. Structs"},{"id":"s5","label":"5. Interfaces"},{"id":"s6","label":"6. Error Handling"},{"id":"s7","label":"7. Packages"},{"id":"s8","label":"8. Goroutines"},{"id":"s9","label":"9. Channels"},{"id":"s10","label":"10. Mutex"},{"id":"s11","label":"11. Context"},{"id":"s12","label":"12. HTTP"},{"id":"s13","label":"13. REST APIs"},{"id":"s14","label":"14. Testing"},{"id":"s15","label":"15. Mock Interviews"},{"id":"review","label":"Interview Review"},{"id":"faqs","label":"FAQ"},{"id":"glossary","label":"Glossary"},{"id":"references","label":"References"},{"id":"disclaimer","label":"Disclaimer"}],"related":[{"title":"Go \u2014 Practice Questions","tag":"Programming","time":"31 min"},{"title":"Go \u2014 Answer Key","tag":"Programming","time":"25 min"},{"title":"Go \u2014 Complete Tutorial","tag":"Programming","time":"55 min"}],"html":"<section id=\"objectives\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Learning Objectives</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Answer 300+ Go interview questions across every experience level.</li>\n          <li>Reason clearly about concurrency, memory, and error semantics.</li>\n          <li>Handle backend system-design follow-ups with confidence.</li>\n          <li>Practice HR and behavioural questions specific to Go teams.</li>\n        </ul>\n        <div class=\"my-4 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-amber-500/40 bg-amber-500/10 text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-100 p-4\"><div class=\"flex items-start gap-3\"><div class=\"mt-0.5 shrink-0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-5 w-5\"><path d=\"M15 14c.2-1 .7-1.7 1.5-2.5 1-.9 1.5-2.2 1.5-3.5A6 6 0 0 0 6 8c0 1 .2 2.2 1.5 3.5.7.7 1.3 1.5 1.5 2.5\"/><path d=\"M9 18h6\"/><path d=\"M10 22h4\"/></svg></div><div class=\"min-w-0 flex-1\"><p class=\"text-sm font-semibold\">How to use</p><div class=\"mt-1 text-sm\">Cover the answer, attempt the question aloud in 60 seconds, then compare. Repeat weekly.</div></div></div></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s1\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">1. Go Fundamentals</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <QA q=\"Why was Go created?\" a=\"To simplify large-scale systems programming at Google: fast compilation, easy concurrency, safe memory management, and a small feature set that scales across large teams.\" />\n        <QA q=\"Is Go interpreted or compiled?\" a=\"Compiled \u2014 to a single static binary, no VM.\" />\n        <QA q=\"What are Go's main design principles?\" a=\"Simplicity, orthogonality, composition over inheritance, explicit over implicit, and 'don't communicate by sharing memory; share memory by communicating.'\" />\n        <QA q=\"Which companies use Go in production?\" a=\"Google, Uber, Dropbox, Cloudflare, Twitch, and the entire cloud-native stack (Docker, Kubernetes, Terraform, etcd, Prometheus).\" />\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1451187580459-43490279c0fa?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 \u2014 Go's place in the modern backend interview: language, concurrency, and cloud infra fluency.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s2\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">2. Variables &amp; Types</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <QA q=\"What's the difference between var and :=?\" a=\"var declares a variable in any scope with optional type and zero value. := is short-form, function-scope only, with inferred type.\" />\n        <QA q=\"What is a zero value?\" a={'The default value assigned when a variable is declared without an initialiser \u2014 0, false, \"\", nil.'} />\n        <QA q=\"Explain iota.\" a=\"A compiler-managed counter reset per const block; used to build enums.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s3\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">3. Functions</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <QA q=\"Can Go functions return multiple values?\" a=\"Yes \u2014 idiomatically (value, error).\" />\n        <QA q=\"What are variadic functions?\" a=\"Functions accepting variable-length arguments via ...T, exposed inside as a slice.\" />\n        <QA q=\"What is a closure?\" a=\"A function value that captures variables from its enclosing scope.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s4\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">4. Structs</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <QA q=\"Does Go have inheritance?\" a=\"No \u2014 it has composition via embedding.\" />\n        <QA q=\"Pointer receiver vs value receiver \u2014 when do you pick?\" a=\"Pointer for mutation, large structs, or consistency across a type; value for small, immutable types.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s5\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">5. Interfaces</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <QA q=\"How are interfaces implemented in Go?\" a=\"Implicitly \u2014 any type with the required method set satisfies the interface.\" />\n        <QA q=\"What's the empty interface?\" a=\"interface{} / any \u2014 satisfied by any type; used for generic containers before generics.\" />\n        <QA q=\"Explain type assertion vs type switch.\" a=\"Assertion checks a single type; a switch checks many with case clauses.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s6\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">6. Error Handling</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <QA q=\"Why does Go not use exceptions?\" a=\"Explicit errors keep control flow visible and force callers to handle failure at the boundary.\" />\n        <QA q=\"Difference between error wrapping and errors.Is / As?\" a={'Wrap with fmt.Errorf(\"\u2026: %w\", err); inspect with errors.Is (identity) or errors.As (typed).'} />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s7\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">7. Packages</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <QA q=\"Difference between package name and import path?\" a=\"Import path is where Go finds the code; package name is what you use in code \u2014 they usually match but need not.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s8\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">8. Goroutines</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <QA q=\"What's a goroutine?\" a=\"A lightweight user-space thread scheduled by the Go runtime, starting at ~2KB stack.\" />\n        <QA q=\"How does the scheduler work?\" a=\"M:N \u2014 M goroutines multiplexed onto N OS threads with a work-stealing scheduler (GMP model).\" />\n        <QA q=\"How do you detect goroutine leaks?\" a=\"Compare goroutine counts before/after tests; use pprof; guarantee every launched goroutine has an exit path.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s9\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">9. Channels</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <QA q=\"Buffered vs unbuffered channel?\" a=\"Unbuffered sends block until a receiver is ready; buffered sends block only when the buffer is full.\" />\n        <QA q=\"What happens when you close a channel twice?\" a=\"Runtime panic.\" />\n        <QA q=\"Receive from nil channel?\" a=\"Blocks forever \u2014 useful for disabling cases in select.\" />\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>select {\ncase v := &lt;-ch: fmt.Println(v)\ncase &lt;-ctx.Done(): return ctx.Err()\n}</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s10\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">10. Mutex</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <QA q=\"RWMutex vs Mutex?\" a=\"RWMutex allows many readers or one writer; use when reads dominate writes.\" />\n        <QA q=\"Channels vs mutexes \u2014 how to choose?\" a=\"Channels for ownership handoff; mutexes for guarding shared state that stays in place.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s11\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">11. Context</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <QA q=\"Why pass context.Context as first arg?\" a=\"Uniform cancellation, deadlines, and request-scoped values across API boundaries.\" />\n        <QA q=\"What NOT to store in context?\" a=\"Business data, authentication credentials, or anything that would be better as an explicit parameter.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s12\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">12. HTTP</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <QA q=\"Is net/http production-ready?\" a=\"Yes \u2014 it's used by many large systems. Configure timeouts explicitly.\" />\n        <QA q=\"How do you write middleware?\" a=\"A function that takes http.Handler and returns http.Handler; wrap with next.ServeHTTP.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s13\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">13. REST APIs</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <QA q=\"How do you version an API?\" a=\"Path prefix (/v1), custom header, or content negotiation. Path is simplest and most cache-friendly.\" />\n        <QA q=\"Idempotency for POST?\" a=\"Add an idempotency key per request, store it server-side, and return the original response on retries.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s14\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">14. Testing</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <QA q=\"What are table-driven tests?\" a=\"A slice of test cases iterated with subtests via t.Run \u2014 the community standard for clarity and coverage.\" />\n        <QA q=\"How do you test concurrent code?\" a=\"Design deterministic tests, use synctest patterns, run with -race, and add stress tests with go test -count=100.\" />\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544197150-b99a580bb7a8?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 2 \u2014 Backend interview architecture: HTTP layer, service layer, repository, database \u2014 with observability at every hop.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s15\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">15. Mock Interviews</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p><strong>Scenario 1.</strong> Design a rate limiter for a public API in Go. Discuss algorithm (token bucket vs sliding window), storage (in-memory vs Redis), and horizontal scaling.</p>\n        <p><strong>Scenario 2.</strong> A goroutine leak is suspected in production. Walk through your triage: metrics, pprof, code review, and remediation.</p>\n        <p><strong>Scenario 3.</strong> Design a URL shortener microservice \u2014 REST API, storage, cache, and analytics pipeline.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"review\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Interview Review</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold\">Top 100 Questions</h3>\n        <p>Master 20 per category (fundamentals, concurrency, HTTP, testing, system design). If you can answer these aloud in under 60 seconds each, you're interview-ready.</p>\n        <h3 class=\"mt-3 font-semibold\">Mock Interview</h3>\n        <p>Pair up: 45 min technical + 15 min behavioural. Rotate weekly.</p>\n        <h3 class=\"mt-3 font-semibold\">Coding Assessment</h3>\n        <p>Solve one small problem live per week \u2014 no IDE completions. Explain trade-offs as you code.</p>\n        <h3 class=\"mt-3 font-semibold\">Interview Checklist</h3>\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>\u2705 Fluent with slices, maps, channels.</li>\n          <li>\u2705 Can spot a race condition in code.</li>\n          <li>\u2705 Can design a small backend end-to-end.</li>\n          <li>\u2705 HR answers rehearsed in your own words.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">FAQ</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>How long should I prepare?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">6\u20138 weeks alongside daily coding \u2014 longer if you're new to Go.</div></details>\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Are LeetCode-style questions asked?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Yes, but usually simpler; interviewers care more about idiomatic Go.</div></details>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"glossary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Glossary</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li><strong>GMP</strong> \u2014 Goroutines, Machines, Processors: Go's scheduler model.</li>\n          <li><strong>Escape analysis</strong> \u2014 compile-time decision of heap vs stack allocation.</li>\n          <li><strong>Backpressure</strong> \u2014 a producer slowing down when the consumer can't keep up.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"references\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">References</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\"><References /></div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"disclaimer\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Disclaimer</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">\n          Interview preparation content is compiled from public sources and community best practices.\n          Real interviews vary widely \u2014 treat answers here as a starting point. Trademarks belong to\n          their respective owners.\n        </p>\n      </div></section>"}